Krita Nova 69 - Freehand selection: stroke smoothing

The Freehand Selection tool's options get a "Stroke smoothing" section, as
the freehand brush has:
- None (as before), Weighted or Stabilizer.
  Weighted: each point of the outline is a Gaussian-weighted average of the
  cursor's path within the distance. Stabilizer: the outline follows the
  cursor on a string of that length, so wobbles shorter than it are left
  out; a dashed line shows the string while drawing.
- Distance: 3-500 screen pixels (default 50), the same at any zoom.
- Finish line (default on): when the pen is lifted, the outline goes on to
  where the cursor is.
Saved in kritarc [KisToolSelectOutline] novaSmoothing,
novaSmoothingDistance, novaSmoothingFinishLine.
The smoothing lives in KisToolOutlineBase (setOutlineSmoothing), off unless
a tool turns it on; only the freehand selection does.

